# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — LIST KIND = CLOSURE-PARAMETER list.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_closure_params_kind`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# Emit site: the `Expr::Closure` arm of `format_expr` -> the delimited-list
# chokepoint `emit_delimited_list("(", ")", ..)` -> `doc::surround_fill`.
#
# Axis cell claim (Core #12 — `list kind x fit` for the CLOSURE-PARAM kind ONLY):
#   cl_empty  empty              `()` — the zero-parameter closure
#   cl_flat   fits-flat          one line, no trailing comma
#   cl_fill   needs-fill         greedy packing at the block continuation indent
#   cl_over   single-over-width  the one closure parameter does not fit on the open
#                                line, so it breaks to the continuation indent — and
#                                being wider than the budget it overflows even there
#
# NOTE the acknowledged, PRE-EXISTING width blind spot this cell also documents:
# the `: <body>` tail is written by the emitter AFTER the Doc is rendered, so it
# is invisible to the packer's fit test and can push the last line past the
# budget. Same shape as `throws` / `:` after a parameter list.
#
# RED source per row: cl_fill / cl_over are TRUE pre-fix REDs (one closure
# parameter per line with a trailing comma, and `): body` hanging off a bare `)`
# line). cl_empty / cl_flat are invariant — break-and-restore them by lowering
# `doc::MAX_WIDTH`.
void cl_empty():
    auto e = (): 0

void cl_flat():
    auto f = (int aaaa, int bbbb, int cccc): aaaa

void cl_fill():
    auto g = (int aaaaaaaa, int bbbbbbbb, int cccccccc, int dddddddd, int eeeeeeee, int ffffffff, int gggggggg, int hhhhhhhh): aaaaaaaa

void cl_over():
    auto h = (VeryLongClosureParameterTypeNameForTheOverWidthCell aSingleClosureParameterWhoseWidthExceedsTheWholeLineBudget): 0
